==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|snottor}}, {{l|ang|snoter}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*snutraz}}, perhaps from the same Indo-European root as Greek [[νοος]] ‘mind’. Cognate with Old High German [[snottar]], Old Norse [[snotr]], Gothic [[𐍃𐌽𐌿𐍄𐍂𐍃]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsnotor/|lang=ang}}

===Adjective===
{{head|ang|adjectives}}

# [[wise]], [[clever]], [[prudent]], [[intelligent]], [[discerning]], [[sagacious]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ang|snotorness}}
* {{l|ang|unsnotor}}

